    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "# SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc – PAYG Readiness Review"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "HowTo"
      },
      "name": "workbook_title"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "# How to use this workbook\n\nThis workbook provides a first technical view of **SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc on Arc-enabled servers**. It is designed to support a PAYG readiness conversation by showing inventory, review scope, validation flags, and exportable evidence.\n\n> This workbook is informational. It does not prove Software Assurance entitlement, Azure billing, CSP recurring PAYG consent, compliance, or final customer approval. Validate billing in Azure Cost Management and validate licensing/commercial decisions through the appropriate customer and licensing process.\n\n## Guide by tab\n\n| Tab | Use it for | Do not use it for |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Summary** | Executive technical footprint: Arc SQL hosts, reported license types, review scope, clean first-wave count, pCore/HADR signals. | Billing, entitlement, or final approval. |\n| **PAYG review scope** | Working list for PAYG review. Use `ReviewScope`, `FirstWaveFit`, `DryRunWouldInclude`, and `ValidationFlags` to decide what can move to a pilot and what needs remediation. | Automatic execution. |\n| **Complete inventory / export** | Full exportable inventory for evidence and reconciliation with dry-run output. | Customer billing proof. |\n| **External validations** | Supporting checks for onboarding tags, missing SQL extension, connected billable SQL hosts, recurring PAYG consent, and SQLServerLicense/pCore resources. | Replacing Cost Management, entitlement validation, or DBA/passive topology review. |\n| **References / execution** | Official Microsoft Learn and GitHub references, plus the recommended dry-run-first execution flow. | Internal-only sales or planning notes. |\n\n## Key fields\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `ReviewScope` | Broad classification of each host for PAYG review. |\n| `FirstWaveFit` | Indicates whether the host is technically clean enough for a pilot after customer/licensing approval. |\n| `DryRunWouldInclude` | Approximation of whether the official script would include the host in `-ReportOnly`; the official dry run remains authoritative. |\n| `HostLicenseType` | License type reported by the Azure Extension for SQL Server: `Paid`, `PAYG`, `LicenseOnly`, or `Not reported`. |\n| `InstanceLicenseTypes` | License/billing signals reported by Arc SQL instances, such as `Paid`, `HADR`, `ServerCAL`, `Free`. |\n| `CoreSignalNotBilling` | Inventory/core signal for prioritization only; not an Azure billing value. |\n| `ValidationFlags` | Required checks before any real change, such as entitlement, ServerCAL, HADR/passive topology, pCore, connectivity, or missing license type. |\n\n## Key outcomes\n\n- `Clean first-wave candidate after commercial approval`: technically cleaner for pilot, but still requires customer/licensing approval.\n- `PAYG review scope with technical flags`: in scope for review, but has blockers or extra checks.\n- `LicenseOnly - inventory only`: do not convert automatically.\n- `Needs LicenseType configuration review`: fix extension/license configuration first.\n- `Paid HA/DR-only - review passive status`: validate passive/DR eligibility before any action.\n\n## Recommended workflow\n\n1. Review **Summary** to understand the environment.\n2. Use **PAYG review scope** to separate clean first-wave candidates from hosts with technical flags.\n3. Export **Complete inventory / export** for the full evidence set.\n4. Run `manage-payg-transition.ps1 -Target Arc -TargetLicenseType PAYG -ReportOnly` for the approved scope.\n5. Reconcile script dry-run output with this workbook and customer/licensing approval.\n6. Pilot a small, approved set and validate `LicenseType = PAYG` plus Cost Management billing.\n7. Scale only after resolving recurring consent, pCore, ServerCAL, passive/HA, connectivity, and entitlement checks."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "HowTo"
      },
      "name": "how_to_customer_safe"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "> **Scope and guardrail**\n>\n> This workbook reads Azure Resource Graph state for **SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc on Arc-enabled servers**. It is a technical readiness and inventory view, not a billing, entitlement, compliance, or approval system.\n>\n> SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc PAYG/Paid/LicenseOnly flows are core-based. If instances report `ServerCAL`, validate the Server+CAL licensing path separately before considering any PAYG transition."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Summary"
      },
      "name": "disclaimer"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.azurearcdata/sqlserverinstances'\n| extend HostId = tolower(tostring(properties.containerResourceId))\n| extend Edition=tostring(properties.edition), Version=tostring(properties.version), InstanceLicenseType=tostring(properties.licenseType), VCore=toint(properties.vCore)\n| extend EditionRank = case(Edition has 'Enterprise', 6, Edition has 'Standard', 5, Edition has 'Web', 4, Edition has 'Express', 3, Edition has 'Developer', 2, Edition has 'Evaluation', 1, 0)\n| extend SqlVersionMajor = case(Version has 'SQL Server 2014' or Version startswith '12.', 'SQL Server 2014', Version has 'SQL Server 2016' or Version startswith '13.', 'SQL Server 2016', Version has 'SQL Server 2017' or Version startswith '14.', 'SQL Server 2017', Version has 'SQL Server 2019' or Version startswith '15.', 'SQL Server 2019', Version has 'SQL Server 2022' or Version startswith '16.', 'SQL Server 2022', Version has 'SQL Server 2025' or Version startswith '17.', 'SQL Server 2025', isnotempty(Version), Version, 'Not identified')\n| summarize Instances=count(), ActiveInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType !~ 'HADR'), HadrInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType =~ 'HADR'), TopEditionRank=max(EditionRank), Editions=make_set(Edition), Versions=make_set(SqlVersionMajor), InstanceLicenseTypes=make_set(InstanceLicenseType), InstanceVCores=sum(VCore) by HostId\n| extend TopEdition = case(TopEditionRank == 6, 'Enterprise', TopEditionRank == 5, 'Standard', TopEditionRank == 4, 'Web', TopEditionRank == 3, 'Express', TopEditionRank == 2, 'Developer', TopEditionRank == 1, 'Evaluation', 'Not identified')\n| extend IsFreeOrTestEdition = TopEdition in ('Developer','Evaluation','Express')\n| extend HadrOnlySignal = Instances > 0 and ActiveInstances == 0\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines'\n    | extend HostId = tolower(id)\n    | project HostId, MachineName=tostring(name), ArcStatus=tostring(properties.status), MachineProvisioningState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), LogicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.logicalCoreCount), PhysicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.coreCount), ResourceGroup=resourceGroup, SubscriptionId=subscriptionId\n) on HostId\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines/extensions'\n    | where tostring(properties.publisher) =~ 'Microsoft.AzureData'\n    | where tostring(properties.type) in~ ('WindowsAgent.SqlServer','LinuxAgent.SqlServer')\n    | extend HostId = tolower(substring(id, 0, indexof(id, '/extensions')))\n    | extend HostLicenseTypeRaw = tostring(properties.settings.LicenseType)\n    | extend HostLicenseType = case(HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'PAYG', 'PAYG', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'Paid', 'Paid', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly', isempty(HostLicenseTypeRaw), 'Not reported', HostLicenseTypeRaw)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw = tostring(properties.settings.UsePhysicalCoreLicense.IsApplied)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = case(UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'true', 'Applied', UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'false', 'Not applied', 'Not reported')\n    | extend RecurringPAYGConsent = tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.Consented)\n    | extend RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp = tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.ConsentTimestamp)\n    | project HostId, ExtensionState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), HostLicenseType, EnableESU=tostring(properties.settings.enableExtendedSecurityUpdates), UsePhysicalCoreLicense, RecurringPAYGConsent, RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp\n) on HostId\n| extend HostLicenseType = coalesce(HostLicenseType, 'Not reported')\n| extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = coalesce(UsePhysicalCoreLicense, 'Not reported')\n| extend EstimatedCoreSignal = coalesce(InstanceVCores, LogicalCoreCount, PhysicalCoreCount, 0)\n| extend ValidationFlags = strcat(\n    iif(ArcStatus !~ 'Connected', strcat('Arc status: ', coalesce(ArcStatus,'Not reported'), '; '), ''),\n    iif(ExtensionState !~ 'Succeeded', strcat('Extension state: ', coalesce(ExtensionState,'Not reported'), '; '), ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'Already reports PAYG; validate billing and recurring consent if CSP-managed; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'PAYG' and RecurringPAYGConsent !~ 'Consented', 'Recurring PAYG consent not reported on extension; required for CSP-managed subscriptions; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'Paid', 'Validate SA or SQL Server Subscription entitlement before change; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly/free/perpetual signal; not automatic PAYG; ', ''),\n    iif(tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes) has 'ServerCAL', 'Server+CAL signal; validate separately before PAYG because Arc PAYG is core-based; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'LicenseType not reported; validate SQL extension configuration; ', ''),\n    iif(UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied', 'pCore/SQLServerLicense signal; validate scope and billingPlan; ', ''),\n    iif(HadrOnlySignal, 'HA/DR-only signal; validate passive eligibility; ', ''),\n    iif(HadrInstances > 0 and ActiveInstances > 0, 'Mixed active + HADR instances; validate HA topology; ', ''),\n    iif(IsFreeOrTestEdition, 'Free/test top edition signal; ', '')\n)\n| extend ReviewScope = case(\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and TopEdition in ('Enterprise','Standard') and ActiveInstances > 0, 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and HadrOnlySignal, 'Paid HA/DR-only - review passive status',\n    HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'Already PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly - inventory only',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'Needs LicenseType configuration review',\n    IsFreeOrTestEdition, 'Free/test edition - inventory only',\n    'Review')\n| extend FirstWaveFit = case(\n    ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG' and ArcStatus =~ 'Connected' and ExtensionState =~ 'Succeeded' and UsePhysicalCoreLicense != 'Applied' and HadrInstances == 0 and tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes) !has 'ServerCAL', 'Clean first-wave candidate after commercial approval',\n    ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG', 'PAYG review scope with technical flags',\n    ReviewScope)\n| extend DryRunWouldInclude = iff(HostLicenseType != 'PAYG' and ExtensionState =~ 'Succeeded', 'Yes - script scope if SQL discovered', 'No')| summarize ArcSQLHosts=count_distinct(HostId), Paid=count_distinctif(HostId, HostLicenseType == 'Paid'), PAYG=count_distinctif(HostId, HostLicenseType == 'PAYG'), LicenseOnly=count_distinctif(HostId, HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly'), NotReported=count_distinctif(HostId, HostLicenseType == 'Not reported'), PaidEntStdReviewScope=count_distinctif(HostId, ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG'), CleanFirstWave=count_distinctif(HostId, FirstWaveFit == 'Clean first-wave candidate after commercial approval'), PcoreSignal=count_distinctif(HostId, UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied'), HadrOnlySignal=count_distinctif(HostId, HadrOnlySignal), MixedHadrActive=count_distinctif(HostId, HadrInstances > 0 and ActiveInstances > 0), ReviewScopeCoreSignalNotBilling=sumif(EstimatedCoreSignal, ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG')",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "First view summary",
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{Subscription}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Summary"
      },
      "name": "summary_metrics"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.azurearcdata/sqlserverinstances'\n| extend HostId = tolower(tostring(properties.containerResourceId))\n| extend Edition=tostring(properties.edition), Version=tostring(properties.version), InstanceLicenseType=tostring(properties.licenseType), VCore=toint(properties.vCore)\n| extend EditionRank = case(Edition has 'Enterprise', 6, Edition has 'Standard', 5, Edition has 'Web', 4, Edition has 'Express', 3, Edition has 'Developer', 2, Edition has 'Evaluation', 1, 0)\n| extend SqlVersionMajor = case(Version has 'SQL Server 2014' or Version startswith '12.', 'SQL Server 2014', Version has 'SQL Server 2016' or Version startswith '13.', 'SQL Server 2016', Version has 'SQL Server 2017' or Version startswith '14.', 'SQL Server 2017', Version has 'SQL Server 2019' or Version startswith '15.', 'SQL Server 2019', Version has 'SQL Server 2022' or Version startswith '16.', 'SQL Server 2022', Version has 'SQL Server 2025' or Version startswith '17.', 'SQL Server 2025', isnotempty(Version), Version, 'Not identified')\n| summarize Instances=count(), ActiveInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType !~ 'HADR'), HadrInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType =~ 'HADR'), TopEditionRank=max(EditionRank), Editions=make_set(Edition), Versions=make_set(SqlVersionMajor), InstanceLicenseTypes=make_set(InstanceLicenseType), InstanceVCores=sum(VCore) by HostId\n| extend TopEdition = case(TopEditionRank == 6, 'Enterprise', TopEditionRank == 5, 'Standard', TopEditionRank == 4, 'Web', TopEditionRank == 3, 'Express', TopEditionRank == 2, 'Developer', TopEditionRank == 1, 'Evaluation', 'Not identified')\n| extend IsFreeOrTestEdition = TopEdition in ('Developer','Evaluation','Express')\n| extend HadrOnlySignal = Instances > 0 and ActiveInstances == 0\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines'\n    | extend HostId = tolower(id)\n    | project HostId, MachineName=tostring(name), ArcStatus=tostring(properties.status), MachineProvisioningState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), LogicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.logicalCoreCount), PhysicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.coreCount), ResourceGroup=resourceGroup, SubscriptionId=subscriptionId\n) on HostId\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines/extensions'\n    | where tostring(properties.publisher) =~ 'Microsoft.AzureData'\n    | where tostring(properties.type) in~ ('WindowsAgent.SqlServer','LinuxAgent.SqlServer')\n    | extend HostId = tolower(substring(id, 0, indexof(id, '/extensions')))\n    | extend HostLicenseTypeRaw = tostring(properties.settings.LicenseType)\n    | extend HostLicenseType = case(HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'PAYG', 'PAYG', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'Paid', 'Paid', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly', isempty(HostLicenseTypeRaw), 'Not reported', HostLicenseTypeRaw)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw = tostring(properties.settings.UsePhysicalCoreLicense.IsApplied)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = case(UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'true', 'Applied', UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'false', 'Not applied', 'Not reported')\n    | extend RecurringPAYGConsent = tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.Consented)\n    | extend RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp = tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.ConsentTimestamp)\n    | project HostId, ExtensionState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), HostLicenseType, EnableESU=tostring(properties.settings.enableExtendedSecurityUpdates), UsePhysicalCoreLicense, RecurringPAYGConsent, RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp\n) on HostId\n| extend HostLicenseType = coalesce(HostLicenseType, 'Not reported')\n| extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = coalesce(UsePhysicalCoreLicense, 'Not reported')\n| extend EstimatedCoreSignal = coalesce(InstanceVCores, LogicalCoreCount, PhysicalCoreCount, 0)\n| extend ValidationFlags = strcat(\n    iif(ArcStatus !~ 'Connected', strcat('Arc status: ', coalesce(ArcStatus,'Not reported'), '; '), ''),\n    iif(ExtensionState !~ 'Succeeded', strcat('Extension state: ', coalesce(ExtensionState,'Not reported'), '; '), ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'Already reports PAYG; validate billing and recurring consent if CSP-managed; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'PAYG' and RecurringPAYGConsent !~ 'Consented', 'Recurring PAYG consent not reported on extension; required for CSP-managed subscriptions; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'Paid', 'Validate SA or SQL Server Subscription entitlement before change; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly/free/perpetual signal; not automatic PAYG; ', ''),\n    iif(tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes) has 'ServerCAL', 'Server+CAL signal; validate separately before PAYG because Arc PAYG is core-based; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'LicenseType not reported; validate SQL extension configuration; ', ''),\n    iif(UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied', 'pCore/SQLServerLicense signal; validate scope and billingPlan; ', ''),\n    iif(HadrOnlySignal, 'HA/DR-only signal; validate passive eligibility; ', ''),\n    iif(HadrInstances > 0 and ActiveInstances > 0, 'Mixed active + HADR instances; validate HA topology; ', ''),\n    iif(IsFreeOrTestEdition, 'Free/test top edition signal; ', '')\n)\n| extend ReviewScope = case(\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and TopEdition in ('Enterprise','Standard') and ActiveInstances > 0, 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and HadrOnlySignal, 'Paid HA/DR-only - review passive status',\n    HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'Already PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly - inventory only',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'Needs LicenseType configuration review',\n    IsFreeOrTestEdition, 'Free/test edition - inventory only',\n    'Review')\n| extend FirstWaveFit = case(\n    ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG' and ArcStatus =~ 'Connected' and ExtensionState =~ 'Succeeded' and UsePhysicalCoreLicense != 'Applied' and HadrInstances == 0 and tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes) !has 'ServerCAL', 'Clean first-wave candidate after commercial approval',\n    ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG', 'PAYG review scope with technical flags',\n    ReviewScope)\n| extend DryRunWouldInclude = iff(HostLicenseType != 'PAYG' and ExtensionState =~ 'Succeeded', 'Yes - script scope if SQL discovered', 'No')| summarize Hosts=count_distinct(HostId), Instances=sum(Instances), ActiveInstances=sum(ActiveInstances), HadrInstances=sum(HadrInstances), CoreSignalNotBilling=sum(EstimatedCoreSignal), PcoreSignals=count_distinctif(HostId, UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied'), HadrOnlySignals=count_distinctif(HostId, HadrOnlySignal), EditionsSet=make_set(TopEdition) by HostLicenseType, ReviewScope\n| extend Editions=tostring(EditionsSet)\n| project-away EditionsSet\n| order by HostLicenseType asc, Hosts desc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "LicenseType and review scope matrix",
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{Subscription}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Summary"
      },
      "name": "license_matrix"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## PAYG review scope\nExport this table for the working review list. Use the **How to use** tab for field definitions and interpretation."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Candidates"
      },
      "name": "review_note"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.azurearcdata/sqlserverinstances'\n| extend HostId = tolower(tostring(properties.containerResourceId))\n| extend Edition=tostring(properties.edition), Version=tostring(properties.version), InstanceLicenseType=tostring(properties.licenseType), VCore=toint(properties.vCore)\n| extend EditionRank = case(Edition has 'Enterprise', 6, Edition has 'Standard', 5, Edition has 'Web', 4, Edition has 'Express', 3, Edition has 'Developer', 2, Edition has 'Evaluation', 1, 0)\n| extend SqlVersionMajor = case(Version has 'SQL Server 2014' or Version startswith '12.', 'SQL Server 2014', Version has 'SQL Server 2016' or Version startswith '13.', 'SQL Server 2016', Version has 'SQL Server 2017' or Version startswith '14.', 'SQL Server 2017', Version has 'SQL Server 2019' or Version startswith '15.', 'SQL Server 2019', Version has 'SQL Server 2022' or Version startswith '16.', 'SQL Server 2022', Version has 'SQL Server 2025' or Version startswith '17.', 'SQL Server 2025', isnotempty(Version), Version, 'Not identified')\n| summarize Instances=count(), ActiveInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType !~ 'HADR'), HadrInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType =~ 'HADR'), TopEditionRank=max(EditionRank), Editions=make_set(Edition), Versions=make_set(SqlVersionMajor), InstanceLicenseTypes=make_set(InstanceLicenseType), InstanceVCores=sum(VCore) by HostId\n| extend TopEdition = case(TopEditionRank == 6, 'Enterprise', TopEditionRank == 5, 'Standard', TopEditionRank == 4, 'Web', TopEditionRank == 3, 'Express', TopEditionRank == 2, 'Developer', TopEditionRank == 1, 'Evaluation', 'Not identified')\n| extend IsFreeOrTestEdition = TopEdition in ('Developer','Evaluation','Express')\n| extend HadrOnlySignal = Instances > 0 and ActiveInstances == 0\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines'\n    | extend HostId = tolower(id)\n    | project HostId, MachineName=tostring(name), ArcStatus=tostring(properties.status), MachineProvisioningState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), LogicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.logicalCoreCount), PhysicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.coreCount), ResourceGroup=resourceGroup, SubscriptionId=subscriptionId\n) on HostId\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines/extensions'\n    | where tostring(properties.publisher) =~ 'Microsoft.AzureData'\n    | where tostring(properties.type) in~ ('WindowsAgent.SqlServer','LinuxAgent.SqlServer')\n    | extend HostId = tolower(substring(id, 0, indexof(id, '/extensions')))\n    | extend HostLicenseTypeRaw = tostring(properties.settings.LicenseType)\n    | extend HostLicenseType = case(HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'PAYG', 'PAYG', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'Paid', 'Paid', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly', isempty(HostLicenseTypeRaw), 'Not reported', HostLicenseTypeRaw)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw = tostring(properties.settings.UsePhysicalCoreLicense.IsApplied)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = case(UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'true', 'Applied', UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'false', 'Not applied', 'Not reported')\n    | extend RecurringPAYGConsent = tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.Consented)\n    | extend RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp = tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.ConsentTimestamp)\n    | project HostId, ExtensionState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), HostLicenseType, EnableESU=tostring(properties.settings.enableExtendedSecurityUpdates), UsePhysicalCoreLicense, RecurringPAYGConsent, RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp\n) on HostId\n| extend HostLicenseType = coalesce(HostLicenseType, 'Not reported')\n| extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = coalesce(UsePhysicalCoreLicense, 'Not reported')\n| extend EstimatedCoreSignal = coalesce(InstanceVCores, LogicalCoreCount, PhysicalCoreCount, 0)\n| extend ValidationFlags = strcat(\n    iif(ArcStatus !~ 'Connected', strcat('Arc status: ', coalesce(ArcStatus,'Not reported'), '; '), ''),\n    iif(ExtensionState !~ 'Succeeded', strcat('Extension state: ', coalesce(ExtensionState,'Not reported'), '; '), ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'Already reports PAYG; validate billing and recurring consent if CSP-managed; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'PAYG' and RecurringPAYGConsent !~ 'Consented', 'Recurring PAYG consent not reported on extension; required for CSP-managed subscriptions; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'Paid', 'Validate SA or SQL Server Subscription entitlement before change; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly/free/perpetual signal; not automatic PAYG; ', ''),\n    iif(tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes) has 'ServerCAL', 'Server+CAL signal; validate separately before PAYG because Arc PAYG is core-based; ', ''),\n    iif(HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'LicenseType not reported; validate SQL extension configuration; ', ''),\n    iif(UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied', 'pCore/SQLServerLicense signal; validate scope and billingPlan; ', ''),\n    iif(HadrOnlySignal, 'HA/DR-only signal; validate passive eligibility; ', ''),\n    iif(HadrInstances > 0 and ActiveInstances > 0, 'Mixed active + HADR instances; validate HA topology; ', ''),\n    iif(IsFreeOrTestEdition, 'Free/test top edition signal; ', '')\n)\n| extend ReviewScope = case(\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and TopEdition in ('Enterprise','Standard') and ActiveInstances > 0, 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and HadrOnlySignal, 'Paid HA/DR-only - review passive status',\n    HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'Already PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly - inventory only',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'Needs LicenseType configuration review',\n    IsFreeOrTestEdition, 'Free/test edition - inventory only',\n    'Review')\n| extend FirstWaveFit = case(\n    ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG' and ArcStatus =~ 'Connected' and ExtensionState =~ 'Succeeded' and UsePhysicalCoreLicense != 'Applied' and HadrInstances == 0 and tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes) !has 'ServerCAL', 'Clean first-wave candidate after commercial approval',\n    ReviewScope == 'Paid Enterprise/Standard - review for PAYG', 'PAYG review scope with technical flags',\n    ReviewScope)\n| extend DryRunWouldInclude = iff(HostLicenseType != 'PAYG' and ExtensionState =~ 'Succeeded', 'Yes - script scope if SQL discovered', 'No')| project MachineName, ReviewScope, FirstWaveFit, DryRunWouldInclude, HostLicenseType, TopEdition, CoreSignalNotBilling=EstimatedCoreSignal, Instances, ActiveInstances, HadrInstances, UsePhysicalCoreLicense, RecurringPAYGConsent, RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp, ArcStatus, ExtensionState, Editions=tostring(Editions), Versions=tostring(Versions), InstanceLicenseTypes=tostring(InstanceLicenseTypes), ResourceGroup, SubscriptionId, ValidationFlags\n| order by ReviewScope asc, FirstWaveFit asc, CoreSignalNotBilling desc, MachineName asc",
